      "markdown": "Pricing methods Prices for goods and services can be established through various methods: market pricing commercial pricing negotiated pricing To establish a commercial price, obtain sufficient price support to validate the offeror\u2019s price. Negotiated pricing is used when a contract requires any type of price negotiations, such as for: a non-competitive contract after a competitive contract has been awarded for aspects not included in the initial financial bids (for example, contract amendments) the use of incentives involving costs See Cost and profit negotiations for more information on pricing methods.",
